{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1908 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "3801c742ae328101eb34df62637dfcee655a020b4dc54b81cb6ae4dc34195fec" :edb/db-before-t 1907 :edb/db-after-t 1908 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535220 50 #inst "2026-10-08T19:50:47.696Z" 13194139535220 true] [17592186087671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338286 13194139535220 true] [17592186087672 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338265 13194139535220 true] [17592186087672 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338272 13194139535220 true] [17592186087672 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338279 13194139535220 true] [17592186088231 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535220 true] [17592186088231 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/assets/c5d36b72e7e2ff6754152a559d64bf3610708c9a2d3790c859bc9abacc9220b6.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." 13194139535220 true] [17592186088231 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/898/Source/Images/q-71978.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." 13194139535220 false] [17592186088231 1145 "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2$ and $\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}.\n$$" 13194139535220 true] [17592186338265 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338266 13194139535220 true] [17592186338265 1089 "q-17519" 13194139535220 true] [17592186338265 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535220 true] [17592186338265 1100 "Write the complex number $z=-4-3\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." 13194139535220 true] [17592186338265 1113 #uuid "6adea076-135d-565e-9953-1bbd05568820" 13194139535220 true] [17592186338265 1145 "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the third quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})| \\\\  & ≈\\pi +0.643\\,50… \\\\  & ≈3.785.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=5$ and $\\theta =3.785$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.785\\,\\text{i}}\\,.\n$$" 13194139535220 true] [17592186338266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338267 13194139535220 true] [17592186338266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338268 13194139535220 true] [17592186338266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338269 13194139535220 true] [17592186338266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338270 13194139535220 true] [17592186338266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338271 13194139535220 true] [17592186338266 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535220 true] [17592186338266 1041 "selection" 13194139535220 true] [17592186338266 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338270 13194139535220 true] [17592186338266 1110 #uuid "48256dd1-ac87-57fa-99ee-1cf29bdfd76f" 13194139535220 true] [17592186338267 1034 "z=5\\,{\\text{e}